1
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,300
Mr. Hui,

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,630
please stop.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,500
Don't think I won't shoot you.

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:14,860
Fire then.

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:17,100
Once I'm dead,

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,460
you'll be completely free of trouble.

7
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,090
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

8
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,290
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

9
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,200
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

10
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,630
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

11
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:18,610
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

12
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:22,770
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

13
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:27,560
♪I'm willing to wait♪

14
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:31,250
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

15
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:34,050
♪I want to share my life with you♪

16
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:40,470
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

17
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:42,620
♪In this cold and gray city♪

18
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,330
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

19
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:46,780
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

20
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:47,440
♪Stay with me♪

21
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:50,190
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

22
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:50,970
♪Stay with me♪

23
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:53,890
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

24
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:56,390
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

25
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:59,430
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

26
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,470
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

27
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:06,690
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

28
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:10,100
[Ash]
[Episoide 1]

29
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,360
Great shot.

30
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:09,490
Let's see who's stronger.

31
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:10,920
I'm stronger.

32
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:14,660
Mr. Wong.

33
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:18,720
Hey, don't just stand here.

34
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,060
Go greet him.

35
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:27,120
What? Not interested in any of them?

36
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,320
I can ask the manager to change them if you want.

37
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:29,720
Feel free to ask me for whatever you want.

38
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,090
Mr. Wong,

39
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:34,160
I'm here to discuss business.

40
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:36,390
Or have you changed your mind?

41
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:37,660
Loek To,

42
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:38,720
don't put it that way.

43
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,220
Everyone in Hong Kong, China, knows no one dares cross you.

44
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,500
[Land Acquisition Proposal]

45
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:53,360
This contract contains the terms we agreed on before.

46
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:58,020
I'll give you the land at the original price plus five percent.

47
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:02,090
After that, Tin Ping Group will handle everything.

48
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:03,820
Sign here.

49
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:09,190
Loek To,

50
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:11,760
don't say I'm not giving you a fair deal.

51
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:13,760
We're all in business

52
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,060
to make money.

53
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:17,560
You say you'll give me five percent more,

54
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:20,160
but Feros offered

55
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:21,790
twenty percent more.

56
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,320
They even said they have a new project they want to do with me.

57
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:26,690
You know how you'd choose.

58
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,990
Feros

59
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,090
has only been in Hong Kong, China, for less than a year.

60
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:36,760
They haven't even released their financial results.

61
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:41,990
Aren't you worried they're making you a promise they can't keep?

62
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,160
Let's not talk about this.

63
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,190
I don't want to ruin our relationship.

64
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,660
If you don't like playing snooker,

65
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:50,620
why don't we go somewhere else?

66
00:05:06,590 --> 00:05:07,490
What?

67
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,460
What do you mean?

68
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:13,560
Mr. Wong, I remember you used to be a Mr. Cheung.

69
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,720
You married into the Wong family

70
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,920
and even changed your surname.

71
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,260
I thought you were deeply devoted to Mrs. Wong.

72
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:25,620
Turns out you only did it to climb the ladder.

73
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,490
You see,

74
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:31,020
my wife isn't a naive woman.

75
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:35,220
You don't think she'll care if I fool around with other women, do you?

76
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:39,420
Of course I know Mrs. Wong is very generous.

77
00:05:40,490 --> 00:05:42,490
She doesn't mind you fooling around outside.

78
00:05:44,790 --> 00:05:47,890
But what if she finds out about this?

79
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,560
Is it really okay, Mr. Wong?

80
00:05:59,090 --> 00:05:59,890
Tell me.

81
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:01,920
What exactly do you want?

82
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:05,720
I told you. I'm here to discuss business.

83
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:07,660
Whether we can reach a deal

84
00:06:09,990 --> 00:06:11,290
is up to you.

85
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:23,540
[Parking Lot Entrance/Exit]

86
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:24,720
Things went pretty smoothly, right?

87
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,620
He's got plenty of dirt on him,

88
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,060
and he still has the nerve to pull tricks.

89
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,690
There's a charity auction tonight.

90
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,190
Not going.

91
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:33,890
What?

92
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,890
I said I'm not going.

93
00:06:37,990 --> 00:06:39,890
Who's the assistant here,

94
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,090
you or me?

95
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:44,620
Either I take you home,

96
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:45,890
or we call it a day right here.

97
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:48,020
So cocky, huh?

98
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,320
Fung!

99
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,560
Run, Boss!

100
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:17,790
Don't run!

101
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,920
I saved the last pineapple bun

102
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:27,960
for you.

103
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,720
Thanks, sir.

104
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:30,220
I'll finish it and leave.

105
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,560
Take your time.

106
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:40,020
Don't go!

107
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:56,500
[Sluggish]

108
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,260
[May Business Prosper]

109
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:23,220
Get up.

110
00:08:24,690 --> 00:08:26,360
This has nothing to do with me.

111
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:35,060
If you're not involved, get out of here.

112
00:08:36,190 --> 00:08:37,890
I don't care about what's going on between you.

113
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:39,260
You ruined my pineapple bun.

114
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,560
How are you going to make it up to me?

115
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:41,960
Enough nonsense.

116
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:43,720
Trying to play the hero, huh?

117
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:59,150
♪Meeting you feels electric. Is it dangerous?♪

118
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:03,240
♪One look sets the whole room on fire♪

119
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:07,600
♪I see secrets flickering in your eyes♪

120
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:11,500
♪Half a second face-to-face, my heart skips a beat♪

121
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,560
♪The dark night tempts my heart♪

122
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:18,130
♪Breath and heartbeat race out of control♪

123
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:22,180
♪Can't wait. I'm going all in♪

124
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:26,580
♪I declare war and break this deadlock♪

125
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:33,030
♪Who takes the bait? Who can walk away?♪

126
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:37,520
♪Prey and hunter lock eyes. Who has the edge?♪

127
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:41,930
♪One pulls back, one moves in, the heat slowly rises♪

128
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,420
Thanks.

129
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,920
I just dealt with a bunch of thugs for a CEO of a listed company.

130
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,960
All I get is a "thanks"?

131
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,220
Do you know who I am?

132
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,720
CEO of Tin Ping Group,

133
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,890
Hui Loek To.

134
00:10:33,290 --> 00:10:35,990
The famous bachelor of the business world.

135
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,060
If I didn't know you,

136
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:38,760
how could I tell people I run with the big boys?

137
00:10:39,490 --> 00:10:40,360
No one will find this place.

138
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:41,120
Sit wherever you like.

139
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:51,160
Hey, where is this?

140
00:10:58,990 --> 00:10:59,620
Come on.

141
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:00,790
I'll clean your wounds.

142
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:02,220
No need.

143
00:11:03,890 --> 00:11:04,760
Take off your vest.

144
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,760
You hurt your back, didn't you?

145
00:11:11,590 --> 00:11:12,620
I said I'm fine.

146
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:14,020
Come on.

147
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,220
Slowly.

148
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,560
That's quite a bad injury.

149
00:11:46,590 --> 00:11:48,590
Does it hurt?

150
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:50,420
Do you know what you're doing?

151
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:52,960
You're afraid of pain, snowflake?

152
00:11:54,590 --> 00:11:55,620
I'm just teasing you.

153
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:04,590
Easy, okay?

154
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:23,220
There you go.

155
00:12:24,390 --> 00:12:25,190
That's it?

156
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,590
What else do you want?

157
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:29,760
This isn't a hospital.

158
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:33,760
Come on. My turn.

159
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,060
Seriously?

160
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:07,690
Darn it.

161
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,590
You're just as afraid of pain.

162
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:11,860
Hurry up.

163
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:34,960
There you go.

164
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:42,620
Didn't expect the CEO to be so thoughtful.

165
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,320
Got a cigarette?

166
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:56,420
Thanks.

167
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,790
Give me one.

168
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:16,860
You hurt your waist, not your hand.

169
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:18,990
I'm hurt all over.

170
00:14:18,990 --> 00:14:21,020
Do you want to check everywhere one by one?

171
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:06,560
Did it burn you?

172
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:07,890
Yeah.

173
00:15:07,890 --> 00:15:08,760
You punk.

174
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:13,970
♪Like we're in love on the edge of a cliff♪

175
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:18,010
♪How thrilling can it really be?♪

176
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:24,340
♪I only win your love by fooling myself♪

177
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,680
♪Love beneath a crumbling wall♪

178
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:32,090
♪Brings far too much heartache♪

179
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,780
♪I hate that I should♪

180
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,440
♪Walk away♪

181
00:16:05,990 --> 00:16:07,490
My car is here.

182
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,320
I never owe anyone

183
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,520
a favor.

184
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,220
How can I contact you?

185
00:16:16,590 --> 00:16:17,690
Cheung Wai Keung.

186
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:28,520
This was my first time meeting Hui Loek To.

187
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,960
Back then, I never imagined

188
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,960
anything would happen between us.

189
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:45,220
[Six months later]

190
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:52,720
[I miss you. Meet you at home.]

191
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,260
Yee Gor.

192
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:22,820
How's the progress?

193
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:24,490
We're rushing the work.

194
00:17:24,590 --> 00:17:25,690
I've called everyone in.

195
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,890
They haven't slept for several days.

196
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:28,160
We'll definitely

197
00:17:28,190 --> 00:17:28,990
get it done for you.

198
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:30,660
Did anyone get sticky fingers?

199
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:33,490
No.

200
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:34,490
No?

201
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,220
Good.

202
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,920
Just kidding.

203
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,620
Tell them if they do a good job

204
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:44,420
this time,

205
00:17:45,090 --> 00:17:46,160
there'll be more work coming.

206
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,720
Got it.

207
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:21,060
[When can we meet?]

208
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:34,560
Mr. Hui,

209
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:38,190
you're only half an hour late today. Punctual.

210
00:18:39,190 --> 00:18:39,990
Let's begin.

211
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,420
The development plan for Bay Area Metropolis

212
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,460
has been revised.

213
00:18:46,790 --> 00:18:48,320
All the materials are here.

214
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:52,020
I've been following this project

215
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:53,190
from the start.

216
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:56,160
All the figures are within reasonable and controllable limits.

217
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:57,990
What's there to change?

218
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,560
Just move forward with it.

219
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:01,820
Here.

220
00:19:02,090 --> 00:19:04,890
I think we can lower the relocation compensation

221
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:06,120
by another ten percent.

222
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:09,420
That'll help us cut costs further

223
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:11,420
and increase the group's profits.

224
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:12,920
Why not?

225
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:16,120
All you ever talk about is increasing profits.

226
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,390
You never consider the risks behind it.

227
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:20,960
The current compensation standards

228
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:23,220
are based on the assessment

229
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:24,390
by Tin Ping Group's professional team.

230
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:26,890
If we cut it by another ten percent,

231
00:19:27,190 --> 00:19:29,060
it'll lead to a strike

232
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:30,060
and delay the project.

233
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:32,960
The losses then will be far more than ten percent.

234
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:36,290
This is Tin Ping's flagship project.

235
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:38,420
We can't cut costs at every turn.

236
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,920
If the residents protest,

237
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:43,160
we'll naturally have ways to deal with them.

238
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,560
Do we really need to care about a few ordinary citizens?

239
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:47,390
Bringing in the gangs again?

240
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:49,990
Are you getting Sheng Tung involved

241
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:50,960
to clear them out overnight

242
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:53,490
and drive them out before they have time to react?

243
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:55,760
You really think the gangs are untouchable?

244
00:20:00,190 --> 00:20:01,660
Hey, anyone inside?

245
00:20:02,190 --> 00:20:04,190
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

246
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:05,760
Let me in and take a look.

247
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:11,520
Are you insane?

248
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:12,790
What else can we do?

249
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:15,720
Hey, anyone inside?

250
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,420
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

251
00:20:25,190 --> 00:20:26,290
Anyone inside?

252
00:20:26,490 --> 00:20:28,090
Coming. Wait a second.

253
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:32,890
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

254
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,160
Let me take a look.

255
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,760
Coming.

256
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:38,620
What's wrong?

257
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:39,420
Hello, sir.

258
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:40,720
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

259
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:41,790
What are you guys doing?

260
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:43,860
I'm so sorry.

261
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,260
I was doing some renovation and burst a water pipe.

262
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,920
I'm taking care of it now.

263
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:49,960
Can you let me in for a look?

264
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,860
I need to report back.

265
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:52,060
There's nothing to see.

266
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,090
Can't you see I'm soaking wet?

267
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:55,660
What? Want to take a shower with me?

268
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,660
I'll fix it right away.

269
00:20:57,820 --> 00:20:59,360
You really have to fix it right away.

270
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:00,460
Otherwise, we'll get another complaint.

271
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,320
It'll be a hassle.

272
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,060
Alright.

273
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:03,190
No problem.

274
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,220
Such a pain.

275
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:16,820
It's done, Yee Gor.

276
00:21:20,290 --> 00:21:21,620
Pretentious.

277
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:24,320
K.

278
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:26,790
Are you sick in the head?

279
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:29,060
You've been in this for years.

280
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:31,460
Your mouth always gets ahead of your brain.

281
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:32,520
How can you be this stupid?

282
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:34,290
Sorry, Yee Gor.

283
00:21:37,260 --> 00:21:38,390
Listen up, everyone.

284
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:40,560
In two nights,

285
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:43,890
we'll be making a deal with Lee Fu.

286
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:45,520
Stay sharp.

287
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:46,860
Don't screw this up.

288
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,360
Got it?

289
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,460
- Got it, Yee Gor. - Got it, Yee Gor.

290
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:54,320
It's not that the gangs are all-powerful.

291
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,120
They can act without regard for the rules.

292
00:21:58,190 --> 00:22:00,990
To deal with this kind of thing, you need to be ruthless

293
00:22:00,990 --> 00:22:02,260
and nip it in the bud.

294
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:04,390
When your dad was still alive,

295
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:07,290
it was that ruthlessness that kept the Hui family standing.

296
00:22:08,990 --> 00:22:10,720
That's how Sheng Tung and Tin Ping

297
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:12,860
grew to the size they are today.

298
00:22:13,590 --> 00:22:14,860
If you keep

299
00:22:14,860 --> 00:22:16,190
worrying about every little thing

300
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,290
and hesitating like this,

301
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:19,990
Tin Ping would've been finished.

302
00:22:20,390 --> 00:22:21,660
Nip it in the bud?

303
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:23,760
What era are we living in?

304
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:26,090
Anyone can upload a video to the Internet on a whim.

305
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:27,260
Then it won't just be the project that's in trouble.

306
00:22:27,290 --> 00:22:29,190
You'll be bringing trouble down on yourself too.

307
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:31,690
Can you bear the consequences?

308
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:33,320
Loek To.

309
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:35,720
Fine.

310
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,960
Who do you think is right?

311
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,460
Me or Vincent?

312
00:22:41,290 --> 00:22:42,290
Mrs. Hui,

313
00:22:42,290 --> 00:22:43,290
you've thought this through carefully.

314
00:22:43,290 --> 00:22:46,020
Lowering the compensation can indeed increase profits.

315
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,090
I've said it many times.

316
00:22:48,460 --> 00:22:49,920
For the Bay Area Metropolis project,

317
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,490
we'll proceed with the plan exactly as I said.

318
00:22:52,290 --> 00:22:53,720
Anyone who still objects

319
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,460
can get out.

320
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:55,860
Yes, Vincent is right.

321
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:57,090
We'll proceed with your plan.

322
00:22:57,090 --> 00:22:59,090
Then we'll go with Vincent's plan.

323
00:22:59,990 --> 00:23:01,520
Since there's nothing to discuss,

324
00:23:02,490 --> 00:23:03,890
we'll do it your way.

325
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:06,620
If anything goes wrong,

326
00:23:06,860 --> 00:23:08,290
you'll be responsible.

327
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:10,920
I'm the CEO.

328
00:23:10,990 --> 00:23:12,620
If anything happens, I'll take responsibility.

329
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:15,760
Have it on my desk by eight tomorrow morning.

330
00:23:15,990 --> 00:23:17,290
If anything goes wrong, I'll hold you accountable.

331
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:18,790
Understood. I'll get it done.

332
00:23:19,890 --> 00:23:20,690
Meeting adjourned.

333
00:23:28,690 --> 00:23:29,520
What else is it?

334
00:23:31,390 --> 00:23:33,220
Your uncle came to see me recently.

335
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:35,790
He said business hasn't been going well lately.

336
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:38,720
He wants to find some work at Sheng Tung's casino.

337
00:23:39,660 --> 00:23:42,660
I was wondering if you could help him get his foot in the door.

338
00:23:43,660 --> 00:23:44,420
What do you think?

339
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:46,660
I don't agree.

340
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:49,720
Third Uncle is a terrible person.

341
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:50,690
He's greedy.

342
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:51,960
Worst of all, he's a gambler.

343
00:23:52,520 --> 00:23:54,720
If we let him join Sheng Tung, it'll only cause trouble sooner or later.

344
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:56,190
And I'll have to clean up the mess again.

345
00:23:57,060 --> 00:23:58,220
I know what you're thinking.

346
00:23:58,790 --> 00:24:00,560
But he's our family.

347
00:24:01,020 --> 00:24:02,590
You have to do this.

348
00:24:03,190 --> 00:24:04,460
If you won't arrange it,

349
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:07,090
I'll have Luk King handle it.

350
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:10,290
Your Third Uncle is very fond of him too.

351
00:24:10,660 --> 00:24:12,090
They get along quite well.

352
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:13,260
No.

353
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:15,160
I've told you before,

354
00:24:15,660 --> 00:24:17,520
Luk King can't get involved in Sheng Tung's business.

355
00:24:17,690 --> 00:24:19,090
He's too honest.

356
00:24:19,090 --> 00:24:20,420
How could he stand up to Third Uncle?

357
00:24:20,590 --> 00:24:22,390
If something goes wrong, what if he gets dragged into it too?

358
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:23,460
I did promise you.

359
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:24,160
So what?

360
00:24:24,820 --> 00:24:26,020
You're a Hui.

361
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:27,820
You have to take responsibility for your own family.

362
00:24:28,420 --> 00:24:30,690
If you won't even help your own uncle,

363
00:24:31,060 --> 00:24:32,420
how will you earn everyone's respect?

364
00:24:33,390 --> 00:24:34,990
If your dad had handled things the way you do...

365
00:24:34,990 --> 00:24:37,160
Stop bringing up Dad every chance you get.

366
00:24:37,390 --> 00:24:39,090
If his way had worked,

367
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:41,760
he wouldn't have left me with such a huge mess after he died.

368
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:43,190
If he was right,

369
00:24:43,260 --> 00:24:45,090
he'd be sitting here today, not me.

370
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:46,990
Then I wouldn't have to go to his grave every year.

371
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:51,320
Do whatever you want.

372
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:52,660
I have nothing more to say.

373
00:25:18,090 --> 00:25:19,520
What's on the schedule next?

374
00:25:20,390 --> 00:25:22,260
We're about to leave for the land auction.

375
00:25:26,090 --> 00:25:26,890
Go on.

376
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:30,960
After that, there's a business reception at the convention center tonight

377
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:34,320
for a Middle Eastern prince opening a family office in Hong Kong, China.

378
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:37,620
Your schedule is packed for the rest of the week.

379
00:25:38,490 --> 00:25:40,190
Do you want me to leave some time for yourself?

380
00:25:44,660 --> 00:25:45,420
No.

381
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:47,820
Let's take care of the important things first.

382
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:48,990
Okay.

383
00:25:59,990 --> 00:26:01,120
Listen up, everyone.

384
00:26:02,190 --> 00:26:03,290
In two nights,

385
00:26:03,690 --> 00:26:06,590
we'll be making a deal with Lee Fu.

386
00:26:06,990 --> 00:26:08,260
Stay sharp.

387
00:26:08,790 --> 00:26:09,560
Don't screw this up.

388
00:26:10,590 --> 00:26:11,090
Two days.

389
00:26:12,860 --> 00:26:13,990
Two days.

390
00:26:22,220 --> 00:26:23,160
You could've come even later.

391
00:26:23,190 --> 00:26:24,720
I'm fine with it. No problem.

392
00:26:29,390 --> 00:26:30,190
Take it off.

393
00:26:43,890 --> 00:26:45,590
Didn't you say you needed to see me urgently?

394
00:26:45,820 --> 00:26:47,020
Don't waste my time.

395
00:26:50,690 --> 00:26:51,520
Go away.

396
00:27:02,220 --> 00:27:03,360
I won't say it twice.

397
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:09,790
If you don't want me touching you,

398
00:27:12,990 --> 00:27:14,160
then don't ask me to come.

399
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:47,020
I told you not to move.

400
00:27:56,420 --> 00:27:57,760
Had enough?

401
00:28:00,990 --> 00:28:02,560
Who's in a hurry now?

402
00:28:21,020 --> 00:28:22,690
Stop moving around.

403
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:35,190
You're pretty bossy, Mr. Hui.

404
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:38,290
If you wanted me to tie you up,

405
00:28:38,860 --> 00:28:40,090
you could've just said so.

406
00:29:08,390 --> 00:29:09,620
Take this off.

407
00:29:16,220 --> 00:29:17,820
You asked for this.

408
00:29:50,490 --> 00:29:52,790
How else am I supposed to take my clothes off?

409
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,620
You don't have to.

410
00:31:57,620 --> 00:31:59,290
Want a beer?

411
00:32:06,190 --> 00:32:07,690
Is beer all you've got?

412
00:32:09,220 --> 00:32:11,120
What else would Young Master Hui like?

413
00:32:12,390 --> 00:32:15,860
Smoked whiskey, made with applewood, oak, and all that...

414
00:32:15,860 --> 00:32:17,090
I don't know anything about smoked whiskey.

415
00:32:17,090 --> 00:32:18,360
It's just a gimmick.

416
00:32:32,590 --> 00:32:33,390
Smoked beer.

417
00:32:34,060 --> 00:32:35,160
You can only get it here.

418
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:43,760
Cheers.

419
00:32:51,420 --> 00:32:52,920
If you want whiskey,

420
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:54,660
I know a pretty famous bar.

421
00:32:55,660 --> 00:32:57,160
We can go together sometime.

422
00:32:57,620 --> 00:32:59,090
Are you asking me out?

423
00:33:00,790 --> 00:33:01,560
Fine.

424
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,220
Forget I said anything.

425
00:33:04,460 --> 00:33:05,990
Don't dodge my question.

426
00:33:07,090 --> 00:33:08,390
Our relationship

427
00:33:08,420 --> 00:33:10,220
only exists between that door and this bed.

428
00:33:11,190 --> 00:33:12,820
Once you walk out, you're nothing to me.

429
00:33:14,420 --> 00:33:15,420
It's just a beer.

430
00:33:15,420 --> 00:33:17,060
Do you have to make it sound so serious?

431
00:33:17,260 --> 00:33:20,260
I can't let people know I'm seeing a thug.

432
00:33:20,260 --> 00:33:21,590
Do you understand?

433
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,090
Am I embarrassing you now?

434
00:33:27,820 --> 00:33:28,760
Yes.

435
00:33:30,990 --> 00:33:32,660
Next time, think it through first

436
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:34,120
before asking me something.

437
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:37,160
Next time?

438
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:40,420
Next time, do it yourself.

439
00:33:40,420 --> 00:33:42,060
What is wrong with you?

440
00:33:45,790 --> 00:33:48,160
The space between the door and the bed

441
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:49,190
isn't our space.

442
00:33:49,190 --> 00:33:50,460
It's your own space.

443
00:33:50,520 --> 00:33:52,860
I can walk out anytime I want.

444
00:33:53,220 --> 00:33:53,820
But you?

445
00:33:53,820 --> 00:33:55,020
Once you walk out that door,

446
00:33:55,020 --> 00:33:56,760
you won't even have the guts to face yourself.

447
00:33:56,790 --> 00:33:58,060
Say that again.

448
00:33:58,260 --> 00:34:00,520
I'll say it. What can you do about it?

449
00:34:02,190 --> 00:34:04,620
You don't even have the guts to go out for a drink.

450
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:47,020
[Cheung Wai Keung: Don't come here anymore.]

451
00:34:52,060 --> 00:34:58,520
[Cheung Wai Keung: Let's all calm down for now.]

452
00:35:38,420 --> 00:35:39,220
Loek To.

453
00:35:42,420 --> 00:35:43,220
What's wrong?

454
00:35:47,390 --> 00:35:49,690
I know you've been busy and under a lot of pressure lately.

455
00:35:50,060 --> 00:35:52,990
If you need any help, just let me know.

456
00:35:53,490 --> 00:35:54,590
What would I ask you for?

457
00:35:55,860 --> 00:35:57,060
Ask me for help.

458
00:36:01,190 --> 00:36:03,390
You should take over some green industries.

459
00:36:03,690 --> 00:36:06,620
Focus on environmental, social, and corporate governance and sustainability.

460
00:36:08,420 --> 00:36:09,090
That kind of thing

461
00:36:09,090 --> 00:36:10,920
can help build the company's brand.

462
00:36:11,420 --> 00:36:14,520
Once I build good relationships with the government and environmental groups,

463
00:36:14,620 --> 00:36:16,560
I'm sure we can solve a lot of problems.

464
00:36:18,190 --> 00:36:18,860
Also,

465
00:36:18,860 --> 00:36:20,290
my team is very capable.

466
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,760
Seriously, if you really need help,

467
00:36:22,790 --> 00:36:23,860
just let me know.

468
00:36:24,020 --> 00:36:26,460
Don't take all the responsibility on yourself.

469
00:36:27,060 --> 00:36:28,660
I can handle the company matters.

470
00:36:31,860 --> 00:36:35,220
Maybe you should stop arguing with Mom.

471
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:41,090
She just wants to save face in front of outsiders.

472
00:36:41,420 --> 00:36:42,320
I know how to handle it.

473
00:36:43,690 --> 00:36:44,790
Okay.

474
00:36:54,100 --> 00:36:55,660
[Police]

475
00:37:04,460 --> 00:37:05,690
Team B, Team C, ready?

476
00:37:07,490 --> 00:37:08,420
Team B's ready.

477
00:37:09,020 --> 00:37:09,920
Team C's ready.

478
00:37:16,260 --> 00:37:18,660
All units, attention. The target is here.

479
00:37:43,420 --> 00:37:44,560
Yee Gor, what's wrong?

480
00:37:50,260 --> 00:37:51,190
Got a light?

481
00:37:56,490 --> 00:37:57,620
There are cops.

482
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:01,920
Where did you get the tip?

483
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:03,320
Are you sure it's reliable?

484
00:38:03,590 --> 00:38:04,920
Of course it's reliable.

485
00:38:04,960 --> 00:38:06,690
We can't go through with the deal tonight.

486
00:38:07,060 --> 00:38:08,590
But if we leave without a word,

487
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:11,490
Lee Fu will get suspicious. That could cause trouble.

488
00:38:11,690 --> 00:38:12,960
Then try telling him

489
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:15,120
we have someone on the police force.

490
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:16,060
Guess what he'll think.

491
00:38:23,690 --> 00:38:26,260
We've got a mole among our own people.

492
00:38:27,020 --> 00:38:28,520
See the exit on the right?

493
00:38:28,990 --> 00:38:30,020
Follow me when we leave.

494
00:38:30,860 --> 00:38:32,560
But we still can't prove

495
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:33,520
whether they actually are...

496
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:35,420
Are you being too naive?

497
00:38:35,790 --> 00:38:37,460
Someone just stabbed me in the back.

498
00:38:37,790 --> 00:38:41,520
Keep this in mind. Don't sweat the small stuff when you're doing big things.

499
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:45,660
Better they sacrifice themselves than I end up dead, right?

500
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:47,060
Got it, Yee Gor.

501
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:50,660
Oi.

502
00:38:51,020 --> 00:38:53,590
Yee Gor and I are going back to the car for something. Stay here.

503
00:38:53,690 --> 00:38:54,690
Don't wander off.

504
00:38:57,260 --> 00:38:58,860
If I find out who the mole is,

505
00:38:58,860 --> 00:39:00,320
I'll make sure he pays dearly.

506
00:39:01,990 --> 00:39:02,690
When this is over,

507
00:39:02,690 --> 00:39:04,020
I'll take you all out for roast goose.

508
00:39:04,690 --> 00:39:05,960
Hey, Yee Gor.

509
00:39:06,520 --> 00:39:07,020
Seriously?

510
00:39:07,060 --> 00:39:09,290
We're already here. Are you leaving without saying hello?

511
00:39:09,290 --> 00:39:10,620
That's not exactly proper, is it?

512
00:39:12,620 --> 00:39:14,060
There are cops everywhere outside.

513
00:39:14,060 --> 00:39:15,220
The deal is off tonight.

514
00:39:16,690 --> 00:39:18,790
Hey, I've got everything ready.

515
00:39:21,890 --> 00:39:22,820
All suspects and goods are in place. Move in.

516
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,490
Seal off all their exits immediately.

517
00:39:24,490 --> 00:39:25,420
Don't let a single one get away.

518
00:39:25,520 --> 00:39:27,020
Fu Gor, Yee Gor wasn't lying to you.

519
00:39:27,060 --> 00:39:28,490
We need to leave now.

520
00:39:28,490 --> 00:39:29,420
No.

521
00:39:29,460 --> 00:39:30,760
I've got the money ready.

522
00:39:30,820 --> 00:39:32,460
I still have customers waiting.

523
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:33,260
The deal has to happen today.

524
00:39:33,860 --> 00:39:34,660
Police!

525
00:39:43,060 --> 00:39:43,720
Run!

526
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:47,890
Run!

527
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:50,890
Don't run!

528
00:39:51,060 --> 00:39:51,690
Don't run!

529
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,120
Come here.

530
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:23,380
[Bullet holes in the wall]

531
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:26,690
Run!

532
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:33,690
Get down! Hands behind your head! Don't move!

533
00:40:36,260 --> 00:40:37,060
Get down!

534
00:40:37,190 --> 00:40:38,060
Cuff him.

535
00:40:52,890 --> 00:40:53,760
Go.

536
00:41:08,390 --> 00:41:09,290
Over there.

537
00:41:10,220 --> 00:41:11,120
Go.

538
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:19,990
Untie this.

539
00:41:35,590 --> 00:41:37,260
Are you kidding? You tied it so tight.

540
00:41:53,860 --> 00:41:54,660
Police!

541
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:35,020
[Friday]

542
00:42:47,620 --> 00:42:49,320
What's on the schedule today?

543
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:56,790
Just say it.

544
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:03,390
Before we start today's schedule,

545
00:43:04,590 --> 00:43:06,490
you might want to take a look at this news report.

546
00:43:08,220 --> 00:43:11,090
Police successfully busted a drug deal last night.

547
00:43:11,220 --> 00:43:13,960
Several suspected core members of a drug-manufacturing ring were arrested.

548
00:43:14,160 --> 00:43:16,290
Among them was a Chinese national surnamed Lee.

549
00:43:16,420 --> 00:43:19,290
Another key member, known as Keung, was shot,

550
00:43:19,290 --> 00:43:20,190
fell into the sea, and remains missing.

551
00:43:20,290 --> 00:43:22,590
Police have deployed divers to search for him.

552
00:43:29,420 --> 00:43:30,220
Hello?

553
00:43:30,290 --> 00:43:30,890
I'm busy right now.

554
00:43:30,890 --> 00:43:31,960
I don't have time to talk.

555
00:43:46,220 --> 00:43:47,460
Find him immediately.

556
00:45:24,020 --> 00:45:24,920
Hello, Boss?

557
